.TH AVR\-ORG\-LIST 1 "" "avr 0.1.2" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-org-list \- List organizations you belong to.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr org list
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List organizations you belong to.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr org list
    avr org list --json slug,role
    avr org list --json '*' -q '.[] | select(.role == "admin")'
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    name, organization_id, role, slug
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-org (1),
.BR avr-org-create (1),
.BR avr-org-email-domain (1),
.BR avr-org-install (1),
.BR avr-org-members (1)
